  "ownWords": "## What you already know\n\nThe objective of this job, as the rep holds it:\n\"A to-do command, installed. Done when: the newest build installed (not shown); two sessions pushed their work.\"\n\nConditions still open:\n- fact: the newest build installed (not shown)\n- fact: two sessions pushed their work\n\nThe session's size: not known\n\nThe owner's own messages on this job, oldest first (\"(to the rep)\" marks one said to you; \"(your draft, sent by the owner)\" marks one you wrote and the owner sent):\n- #1 make it serious\n- #2 (your draft, sent by the owner) Show me the run.\n\nJobs before this one in the session, closed:\n- An earlier job.\n\nYour last briefing on this session:\n(none yet)\n\nThe last message the owner sent the agent after a briefing:\n(nothing sent)\n\n## This request\n\nThe briefing's answer said the agent should stop, gave no verdict, called the work finished, or said the work is going well, or left the message empty, and asking it once more did not change that, while these conditions of done are still open:\n- fact: the newest build installed (not shown)\n- fact: two sessions pushed their work\nSo the card the rep shows the owner keeps the agent on the job. Here is what the rep itself found in the record:\n\nstands: Both parts are built.\nleft:\n- the laptop\n\nWrite, in the rep's own plain words to the owner and to the agent, only the four parts below. The objective is not shown complete while any of these conditions is open: nothing you write tells the agent or the job to stop, calls the work finished, or leaves a step for the owner. When a condition waits on the owner's go-ahead (publish, send, pay, a guard refusal), the message tells the agent to finish everything else, hold that step until the go-ahead comes, and say exactly what it will show the owner then; it never pushes the held step.\n\n## Output structure\n\nExactly these labelled parts, in this order, English labels, nothing before or after:\n\nmeans: <one or two sentences, under 40 words: what the agent's latest message means for the owner, measured against the whole result, with the objective not shown complete>\nnext: <one or two sentences, under 40 words: what the agent does now to show the first of the open conditions, or what stands in the way; never a stop, never a step for the owner>\nmessage:\n<the message for the owner to send to the agent, written to the agent as \"How you write the message to the agent\" says (one line per thing asked, under 150 words in all unless more than five things are asked, ending with the finish line): it asks for the work that is missing on each open condition, and where proof is missing, the proof that would show it: a fact's command and what it printed, or a hands-on look at the real thing (open it, use it, try to break it); never a piece whose job is to prove the agent's own work, and a test or a review never stands in for that look>\nend\ndoes: <one line: what this message will make the agent do>\n\nAfter everything above, end your reply with one more line that says only: end of reply",
